{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan","id":1503530,"title":"The Warrior Caste should not have been able to take control of the Assamite Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-20T10:24:15-08:00","id":1503530,"title":"The Warrior Caste should not have been able to take control of the Assamite Clan","content":"V20 lore of the clan states that the Warrior clan was able to take control of the Assamites because they had superior numbers and fighting skills. What I don't understand is how the other castes could simply let that happen. The Visers I can kind of understand, they were diplomats, not fighters, but the sorcerer caste is a whole different story. The sorcerers had something that is coveted by almost every vampire, Blood Magic, their specific school was called dur-an-khi. The paths found within this school of blood magic include Spirit manipulation, lure of flames, movement of the mind, path of conjuring, Path of warding, Weather control, and many more.<br /> <br /> Auspex was at one time an in-caste discipline for the sorcerers, so they probably had a good amount of people running around with Auspex 5, which allows you to use the powers from many different paths, all from the safety of the astral plane. Combining that with path of Spirit manipulation, they could perhaps create a sizable army that they could summon at a moment's notice against the warriors, all of which can be done from a safe distance away. And IMO, if the school of blood magic you practice requires you to, as stated in the wiki, &quot;call upon ancient covenants with spirits&quot; to fulfill your desires, then Spirit Manipulation better be a primary path for every sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Something, else that irks me is that the reason the warriors have a much larger number of embraces than the other two in the early nights of the clan, is that it was hard for the visors and the sorcerers to find individuals with the right qualities, such as political skill or occult knowledge. If that were the case wouldn't it be best to simply... teach them? Instead of waiting around hoping to find someone who miraculously possesses the qualities you are looking for, it would be far better if each Viser or Sorcerer, took at least 1-2 young apprentices and taught them what they needed to know, as well as prep them for the embrace. They could even create classrooms to teach these kids. Nothing too big, but enough to grow their numbers.<br /> <br /> What do you think?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T11:36:01-08:00","id":1503537,"title":"","content":"There's a reason for the inaction of the sorcerers during the warriors takeover, and ironically, it's dur-an-khi itself.<br /> <br /> If you're interested, it's mentioned in both pre V20 books on blood magic.<br /> <br /> See, for practitionners of dur-an-khi, the way to learn more paths is through an exctatic trance caused either by vitae laced drugs or other methods, once in this trance, the sorcerer enter a vision of a realm they call the stair to heaven, which is composed of massive stairs where the sorcerer faces mental trials and meet with spirits representing gods to negociate with them for blood magic powers.<br /> <br /> But the stair also contain what the sorcerer caste call stations, massive places symbolizing the planets and their influence , and the sorcerers' goal is to attain the eighth and last one, which they believe will offer them either absolute power or some form of transcendance.<br /> <br /> The thing is, for millenias, they were blocked at the moon station, which appears as a paradise. It is some spiritual trap, keep the sorcerer enamoored in sensual pleasure to delay his quest of further revelations.<br /> <br /> But the sorcerers though that this place was actually the promised heaven, so they spent millenias in trance, spending their time in the arms of spiritual concubines, until very recently ( the books doesn't precise exactly when) a debate amongs caste led to the discovery that this was not heaven, but just a first step, and that ignoring the pleasures of the station led to new levels of the stair.<br /> <br /> So in resume, the warriors were able to take over because the vizirs were simply diplomats, scholars and bureaucrats, and because the sorcerers were partying for the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:12:51-08:00","id":1503542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503537#post1503537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason for the inaction of the sorcerers during the warriors takeover, and ironically, it's dur-an-khi itself.<br /> <br /> If you're interested, it's mentioned in both pre V20 books on blood magic.<br /> <br /> See, for practitionners of dur-an-khi, the way to learn more paths is through an exctatic trance caused either by vitae laced drugs or other methods, once in this trance, the sorcerer enter a vision of a realm they call the stair to heaven, which is composed of massive stairs where the sorcerer faces mental trials and meet with spirits representing gods to negociate with them for blood magic powers.<br /> <br /> But the stair also contain what the sorcerer caste call stations, massive places symbolizing the planets and their influence , and the sorcerers' goal is to attain the eighth and last one, which they believe will offer them either absolute power or some form of transcendance.<br /> <br /> The thing is, for millenias, they were blocked at the moon station, which appears as a paradise. It is some spiritual trap, keep the sorcerer enamoored in sensual pleasure to delay his quest of further revelations.<br /> <br /> But the sorcerers though that this place was actually the promised heaven, so they spent millenias in trance, spending their time in the arms of spiritual concubines, until very recently ( the books doesn't precise exactly when) a debate amongs caste led to the discovery that this was not heaven, but just a first step, and that ignoring the pleasures of the station led to new levels of the stair.<br /> <br /> So in resume, the warriors were able to take over because the vizirs were simply diplomats, scholars and bureaucrats, and because the sorcerers were partying for the ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I do remember reading about that, been a while though. This makes it sounds like an extremely ineffecient way to learn blood magic in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So to learn anything new, you need to climb the stairs and do that whole song and dance? No wonder the vampires in europe and asia stopped using dur-an-khi. Sheesh, at that point I think I would rather join the Trimira in India and learn Sadhana, from what I read they accept anyone as long as they willingly allow themselves to be blod bound to the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-20-2023, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:57:55-08:00","id":1503552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503542#post1503542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I do remember reading about that, been a while though. This makes it sounds like an extremely ineffecient way to learn blood magic in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So to learn anything new, you need to climb the stairs and do that whole song and dance? No wonder the vampires in europe and asia stopped using dur-an-khi. Sheesh, at that point I think I would rather join the Trimira in India and learn Sadhana, from what I read they accept anyone as long as they willingly allow themselves to be blod bound to the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, I don't think european and asian vampires ever learned dur an khi, at least in the way the assamite do.<br /> <br /> I think there's both positives and negatives to that form of magic<br /> <br /> On the negatives, you're entirely right, going on vision question to bargain with spirits is far less efficient than opening heavy tomes of thaumaturgy or listening to a powerful mentor.<br /> <br /> On the other side, the principles of the ladder of heaven means that any kindred who knows how to enter the trance can potentially obtain every conceivable form of blood magic on their own without depending on another source like tremere's chantries or the researchs of a koldun.<br /> <br /> And secondly, although it is a topic criminally underdevelloped by white wolf, it is mentioned that the stations further than the moon's own offer specific advantages for the sorcerer than spiritually enter them.<br /> <br /> The only specified one is the station right after the moon, the representation of mercury, in which, simply by mentally &quot;standing&quot; there, the sorcerer can tap into global communication and surveillance networks.<br /> <br /> Although this led to some fear amongs assamites, as the sorcerers who attained the station swears that they hear satellites whispers to each others, and wonder if the internet isn't becoming sentient.<br /> <br /> Cue the glass walkers and virtual adepts snarks &quot;first time, right?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T14:49:05-08:00","id":1503569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503552#post1503552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> To be fair, I don't think european and asian vampires ever learned dur an khi, at least in the way the assamite do.<br /> <br /> I think there's both positives and negatives to that form of magic<br /> <br /> On the negatives, you're entirely right, going on vision question to bargain with spirits is far less efficient than opening heavy tomes of thaumaturgy or listening to a powerful mentor.<br /> <br /> On the other side, the principles of the ladder of heaven means that any kindred who knows how to enter the trance can potentially obtain every conceivable form of blood magic on their own without depending on another source like tremere's chantries or the researchs of a koldun.<br /> <br /> And secondly, although it is a topic criminally underdevelloped by white wolf, it is mentioned that the stations further than the moon's own offer specific advantages for the sorcerer than spiritually enter them.<br /> <br /> The only specified one is the station right after the moon, the representation of mercury, in which, simply by mentally &quot;standing&quot; there, the sorcerer can tap into global communication and surveillance networks.<br /> <br /> Although this led to some fear amongs assamites, as the sorcerers who attained the station swears that they hear satellites whispers to each others, and wonder if the internet isn't becoming sentient.<br /> <br /> Cue the glass walkers and virtual adepts snarks &quot;first time, right?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats actually a pretty interesting concept. Its sad that we may never see this explored further though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-20-2023, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T17:26:03-08:00","id":1503576,"title":"","content":"I think there may also be a difference between game-mechanics and how things work in-story here. In game-mechanics, learning to become a soldier costs exactly as much as learning to be a wizard. In-story things may be a bit different, with almost anyone being able to get through basic training, but only a few people having that spark of genius needed to become a wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T18:37:08-08:00","id":1503585,"title":"","content":"When the metapplot rears its ugly head, it's likely because the Warrior Caste didn't just wake up and decide to take over the running of the clan one day on its own, but were the faction whose goals and methods aligned best with Ur-Shulgi's. You know, the ancient monstrosity whose descendants include 2/3 of the Sorcerer Caste?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T23:42:29-08:00","id":1503601,"title":"","content":"I think it makes a lot of sense. No, I think it makes perfect sense and was inevitable.<br /> <br /> Ideally, the viziers serve to infiltrate, scout, finance and facilitate warrior and sorcerer activities in their area. The idea that they're scholars really means &quot;good with money&quot; &quot;good with politics&quot; and &quot;good at mingling with polite society&quot;<br /> <br /> The warriors could also do that, or at least, they've the idea that they can purge an increasingly liberalizing vizier class and repopulate them with loyalist viziers. The new loyalist Aassamites are more radical and don't plan to be discriminating that much with their targets, so if their vizier replacements aren't as good it doesn't really matter as much.<br /> <br /> As for sorcerers<br /> -Assamite sorcerers are spread thin. They're rare and their services are demanded in a wide range.<br /> -They aren't anywhere near as unified as Tremere, the way they practice magic differs substantially from sorcerer to sorcerer, and thus big internal divisions are likely.<br /> -Assamite sorcerers are entirely dependent on the other two castes. Not only are they the main customers, but they also provide the resources and security needed for their operations<br /> -few sorcerers are leader types. They're smart people, but bothering with that kind of thing will take time away from magical studies. It makes sense to let the other castes take the lead.<br /> -Ur-shulgi is the OG assamite sorcerer, him rising is theoretically a good thing for them.<br /> -The <b>anti-religion rhetoric of the loyalist faction is a good thing for them; </b>Islam stifles Dur-An-Ki so any pushback is welcomed.<br /> -Fighting the warriors is fucking stupid. You'd need your trade to exceed 10-for-1. Warriors have a wide talent pool to choose from, sorcerers don't, so 10 for 1 would become insufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-21-2023, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T01:42:19-08:00","id":1503604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503585#post1503585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the ancient monstrosity whose descendants include 2/3 of the Sorcerer Caste?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Ur-Shulgi would hardly be the first ancient vampire to decide that its descendants are doing things wrong and need to be purged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T12:01:12-08:00","id":1503626,"title":"","content":"Sorry for sounding clueless, but I thought Ur-Shulgi was killed off by the SI. At the very least, isn't he in, or at least near, ground zero for the Gehenna War?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T15:34:35-08:00","id":1503635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503626#post1503626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for sounding clueless, but I thought Ur-Shulgi was killed off by the SI. At the very least, isn't he in, or at least near, ground zero for the Gehenna War?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think we have been told anything as of yet with ur-shulgi, wonder if they will go in depth with what happens during the gehenna war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T15:36:02-08:00","id":1503636,"title":"","content":"The warrior caste &quot;took control&quot; of the Assamites because originally they were the only Assamites. It was not until Revised that concepts like the castes and the Viziers and Sorcerers were established. So they were added retroactively to continuity. We then now had the issue of who were these other castes, what were they doing beforehand, and why we had not known about them before. This lore exists just to explain this retroactive continuity which is why we now have &quot;history&quot; like this. It is completely an OOC need to reconcile the retcon with canon. It's not something that was organic IC.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the new explanation as to why the warrior caste was previously dominant, go with what you think best if you are STing a chronicle. The only person you need to make happy is yourself (and your gaming group).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T19:01:13-08:00","id":1503660,"title":"","content":"If you really NEED an in-universe rationalization for an out-of-universe retcon, consider that the other castes probably didn't WANT to have a war with the Web of Knives. Who would? The Warrior caste are the ones who <i>specialize in murder </i>- specifically murder of other vampires - and the Web of Knives are the most enthusiastic about it.<br /> <br /> It's not a big stretch to assume when the Web of Knives stared asserting themselves, the Vizier and Sorcerer castes were willing to go along with their policies because it was easier that getting into a fight. By and large, the extremists were directed OUTWARD, at non-Assamites. History has shown us that moderates will readily let the extremists do what they like, so long as it doesn't put themselves at risk.<br /> <br /> (Brief aside: not only are Sorcerers a smaller caste than Warriors, they're also way harder to make. A newly Embraced member of the Sorcerer caste probably had little to no magical knowledge or skill prior to that. Whereas the Warrior caste can pick any soldier, killer, or even brigand off the streets and be partway to making them an Assamite Warrior. They don't need years of tutelage just to get any results at all, post-Embrace. So while Sorcerers have an innate skill bottleneck, the Warriors don't have that problem. They would ALWAYS outnumber them. Viziers, meanwhile, have neither combat nor magical experience, most times, so they don't contribute much during an actual fight. Logistics, sure, but not when swords start swinging.)<br /> <br /> Another angle one might consider is that non-extremist Assamites, outside the Web of Knives, probably still felt humiliated after the Anarch Revolt and the resulting Tremere Curse. The Clan not only got beaten, but got their Clan shackled. Sure, many Assamites probably didn't care much about not being able to Diablerize. But it's the principle of the matter.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer caste especially would feel humiliated. They were bested by upstart hedge magicians in the field of the arcane, in a curse they couldn't wriggle out of. Imagine you're an Assamite Sorcerer, heir to magical praxis made perfect in the days of Suleiman the Wise. Now imagine some foreign peddler of cheap charms, whose lineage started a mere few centuries ago and was STOLEN from multiple separate Clans (in various capacities), got the right to lay a hex on you that you couldn't subsequently break. No matter what rites you performed or how you meditated.<br /> <br /> You'd probably feel bitter, angry, and spiteful enough to listen to the fanatics in the Warrior caste preaching a holy war. You take the devil's bargain, because your pride as a magician won't allow you to let that grudge go.<br /> <br /> It would take centuries, and the heightening of extremism to the point the Sorcerers and Viziers felt threatened, for them to break with the Web of Knives. Especially when Ur-Shulgi breaks the Tremere Curse seemingly effortlessly (it was actually a rather involved ritual, but Ur-Shulgi pulled it off very quickly after returning, when centuries of Sorcerer caste work couldn't). Without the Diablerie replacement the Sorcerers held as a bargaining chip, their position relative to the Web of Knives becomes significantly less secure. (The exact order of events is unimportant. Just the threat of Ur-Shulgi breaking the curse is enough to make non-fanatic Assamites reconsider the nature of their relationship.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T22:02:20-08:00","id":1503663,"title":"","content":"Basically what Bluecho told above. You dont mess with a bunch of psycho murders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T08:17:08-08:00","id":1503814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503626#post1503626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for sounding clueless, but I thought Ur-Shulgi was killed off by the SI. At the very least, isn't he in, or at least near, ground zero for the Gehenna War?</div> </div> </div> </div>nope,according to a opp v5 book,a official one. he's undead and well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T08:29:41-08:00","id":1503815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503576#post1503576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there may also be a difference between game-mechanics and how things work in-story here. In game-mechanics, learning to become a soldier costs exactly as much as learning to be a wizard. In-story things may be a bit different, with almost anyone being able to get through basic training, but only a few people having that spark of genius needed to become a wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't remember in story indications that becoming a sorcerer requires anything more than learning","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T08:33:49-08:00","id":1503816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503660#post1503660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer caste especially would feel humiliated. They were bested by upstart hedge magicians in the field of the arcane, in a curse they couldn't wriggle out of. Imagine you're an Assamite Sorcerer, heir to magical praxis made perfect in the days of Suleiman the Wise. Now imagine some foreign peddler of cheap charms, whose lineage started a mere few centuries ago and was STOLEN from multiple separate Clans (in various capacities), got the right to lay a hex on you that you couldn't subsequently break. No matter what rites you performed or how you meditated.<br /> e</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sorcerer caste allowed the tremere curse to happen. Their leader was thankful for it, since it chained down the web of knife and forced them to be dependant on the sorcerers for rites to lower generation.<br /> <br /> There's a dialogue between the Amr of the sorcerers and a tremere in the beckett jyhad diary on the matter. Basically, the amr mock the presumptousness of the tremere, considering them as little more than arrivists without real depth<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T10:20:45-08:00","id":1503822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503815#post1503815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't remember in story indications that becoming a sorcerer requires anything more than learning</div> </div> </div> </div>In many <i><b>World of Darkness</b></i> books it is noted, described, and detailed that specific kinds and ways of spellcasting might have very specific and relatively high requirements in regard to skills, knowledge, wisdom. And also in regard to resources and items which are distinctly needed.<br /> Blood Magic as practiced by the Kindred - including Tremere Thaumaturgy, Giovanni Necromancy, Assamite Sorcery, and other types and ways of Blood Magic - does seem to definitely be included, outlined, and described within these requirements, circumstances, and categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T22:22:15-08:00","id":1503877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503815#post1503815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember in story indications that becoming a sorcerer requires anything more than learning</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I don't think that's exactly true in the case of Assamite sorcerers. Assamite sorcerers are spread thin and their small numbers likely mean they're somewhat overworked, their sorcery isn't standardized at all so many aren't practicing compatible skills. Having a strong preference for people already one-foot in the door when it comes to magic is a great time saver, while it does also contribute to what makes the Assamite sorcerers such a mess. <br /> <br /> Politically, it also does good to keep Sorcerers embracing magicians because it keeps the caste divided under different practices. If you had one sorcerer who started to train new sorcerer batches in a unified manner it would be terrible for everyone. Other magicians would fear their practices would become obsolete in the face of a standardized Assamite caste, while viziers and warriors would have a problem with ascendant sorcerers. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T10:12:38-08:00","id":1503901,"title":"","content":"Ur-Shulgi has been keeping a low profile since he broke the clan curse and caused the fracturing of the clan. As it stands from the Camarilla sourcebook that dealt with Banu Haqium more or less states he isn't gone and elders like Fatahma are concerned what his next move is and predicting the moves of an ancient potent child is hard at the best of times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T12:35:31-08:00","id":1503912,"title":"","content":"I love the totally wrong assumption that whenever an ancient wakes up they need to start making big moves and stuff. Vampires are very local creatures. They pick a city and they don't really move much beyond that. In any case, why not chill? A thaumaturge in particular is more likely to just catch up with what they've missed and work on some cool rituals with the new data they have. Imagine Ur-Shulgi trying to reverse engineer a tablet and working out how he can use it for spells, or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T14:22:04-08:00","id":1503965,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t that one of them conceits that elders and ancients being concerned about far off locales when they would be more worried about there own fiefdoms? Personally why would Arch Bishop Moncada of Madrid be interested in the affairs of Polina of New York when he would wanting to keep things stable in his own backyard? It always struck me as odd, but it was part of the setting and went with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T18:39:55-08:00","id":1503975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503626#post1503626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for sounding clueless, but I thought Ur-Shulgi was killed off by the SI. At the very least, isn't he in, or at least near, ground zero for the Gehenna War?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, the canonical fate of Ur-Shulgi is he left for... somewhere.<br /> <br /> Though the Sabbat book indicates it was a Salubri that killed him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503912#post1503912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the totally wrong assumption that whenever an ancient wakes up they need to start making big moves and stuff. Vampires are very local creatures. They pick a city and they don't really move much beyond that. In any case, why not chill? A thaumaturge in particular is more likely to just catch up with what they've missed and work on some cool rituals with the new data they have. Imagine Ur-Shulgi trying to reverse engineer a tablet and working out how he can use it for spells, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I was there when Ur-Shulgi woke up, at least in terms of being a V:TM fan heavily plugged into the social media of the time period. The whole point of Ur-Shulgi was that he was a Harbinger of Gehenna because he DIDNT act like other Methusalehs. For the previous history of the tabletop game, Methuselahs were always INVISIBLE.<br /> <br /> They hid behind proxies and proxies.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi's thing was...he didn't...and it was a sign Gehenna was near.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-26-2023, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T20:46:18-08:00","id":1503978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503530-the-warrior-caste-should-not-have-been-able-to-take-control-of-the-assamite-clan?p=1503975#post1503975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I was there when Ur-Shulgi woke up, at least in terms of being a V:TM fan heavily plugged into the social media of the time period. The whole point of Ur-Shulgi was that he was a Harbinger of Gehenna because he DIDNT act like other Methusalehs. For the previous history of the tabletop game, Methuselahs were always INVISIBLE.<br /> <br /> They hid behind proxies and proxies.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi's thing was...he didn't...and it was a sign Gehenna was near.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. Some of the first Methuselahs VtM fans were exposed to were Helena and Menele. Two characters whose presence in Chicago were deep secrets, that players weren't meant to find out until well into a Chicago campaign. Even though, in the case of Helena, the PCs likely <i>met her</i> well before learning who she really was.<br /> <br /> That was the point. The Kindred world was a series of concentric circles of secrecy and conspiracy, with Neonate PCs being initiated into the outermost layer (namely &quot;Vampires exist, and you're now one of them&quot;) and having to fight fang and claw to learn more. Most Elders in the setting were unaware just how much <i>their</i> elders were pulling strings behind the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}